&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Real Chemistry is looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt; to join our global Patient Advocacy team. This client-facing role is ideal for a highly organized healthcare communications professional who is ready to help deliver meaningful patient advocacy programs across pharmaceutical, biotechnology, medical device and health technology clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;SAE&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;will support the development and execution of integrated advocacy programs, manage day-to-day client and stakeholder activity, contribute to high-quality materials and scopes, and help ensure work is delivered on time, on budget and to Real Chemistry standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and execution of advocacy strategies aligned to brand, policy, access, and disease-area objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to authentic, ethical and compliant engagement with patient advocacy organizations, coalitions and community leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design and deliver patient-centric programs, including education, awareness, policy engagement, advisory boards, summits, co-creation sessions, and community-based initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide exceptional client service and account management support across multiple client accounts and workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted day-to-day client contact for planned activities, ad hoc requests, project updates and delivery of materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new business development, pitches and proposals, and identify opportunities to evolve or expand client programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently working as SAE, or strong AE ready to step up in a patient advocacy agency, or patient advocacy team within a comms agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with, or supporting programs involving, patient advocacy organizations, patient communities, NGOs, coalitions or healthcare stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global advocacy experience is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and oral communication skills, including formal and informal presentations and confident participation in client-facing conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to draft clear project scopes, client and vendor contracts, presentations, briefs, communications materials and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office tools, especially PowerPoint, Word and Excel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable conducting research, monitoring relevant media or landscape developments, and contributing to insight-led client recommendations with limited supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note: this role requires hybrid working with 2 days per week from one of our offices - London, Manchester or Edinburgh.&lt;/p&gt;
