&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is an award-winning communications consultancy that advises enterprises, institutions, and individuals on building recognition and enhancing reputation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;From our offices across Europe and the Middle East, we adopt an integrated approach that connects the dots across channels, audiences and issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our collective of smart, curious people think differently and live by a shared mission, purpose, vision, and values. These shape how we work, not just with our colleagues, but with clients and partners too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to ‘rewire communications for impact’ and harness its transformative power to advocate, trailblaze and make a difference.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We do this by igniting and empowering the potential of every individual within our company, recognising that each person is a unique spark, capable of creating extraordinary impact. We believe that by nurturing and harnessing the collective brilliance of our people, we can drive innovation, foster an uncommon work culture, and make a positive difference to society.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Embracing the complete range of skills and services across the communications spectrum without constraint, we create the best outcomes for our clients and deliver world-class work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hanover is looking for an experienced public affairs professional to join our growing Advocacy team in London.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will be a senior member of our market-leading public affairs practice and will have the opportunity to lead account teams, advise senior clients, contribute to new business activity and shape team management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will join our award-winning, market-leading, public affairs practice, working with a team of political specialists to advise some of the world&#39;s biggest brands on UK political and regulatory issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re particularly keen to hear from candidates with prior agency or in-house experience and a passion for one or a mix of our key sectors, including Financial Services, Creative Industries and Energy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is one of the UK’s leading communications consultancies. Our consultants work in a fast-paced, rapidly evolving environment, and are equally comfortable in the office, at a pitch or at a networking event. We also enjoy being an extension of our clients&#39; in-house teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted adviser to senior clients, developing strong relationships and providing strategic counsel on political, policy and regulatory issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of effective public affairs strategies, translating complex political and regulatory developments into clear, actionable recommendations for clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead client meetings and oversee the delivery of high-quality presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain consistently high standards across client work across multiple accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop junior team members, supporting their performance, progression and professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and project manage new business activity, including proposals and pitching, and identify opportunities to grow existing client relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a strong network of business, policy, political and industry contacts, representing Hanover at relevant events and developing relationships that generate insight and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor emerging political, regulatory and industry trends, helping clients anticipate change and positioning Hanover as a source of informed, forward-looking counsel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Hanover&#39;s external profile and thought leadership, including developing relevant content and sharing expertise on key policy and political issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with colleagues across Advocacy and the wider business to deliver integrated communications strategies and share knowledge and best practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take commercial ownership of accounts, including oversight of budgets, team resource and profitability, ensuring work is delivered efficiently and to a high standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very strong team-working, collaboration and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant public affairs experience within a consultancy, government or in-house team, with experience operating at a senior level. The ability to manage integrated PA/comms campaigns is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong policy background in one or more of our key sectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent knowledge of and passion for UK politics and the regulatory environment, with a demonstrable understanding of their impact on business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong account and project management skills, with experience overseeing multiple workstreams and maintaining consistently high standards of client delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience of business development, including pitches, proposals/RfPs and identifying opportunities for organic growth and cross-selling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring and developing colleagues and providing effective quality control and direction to account teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial awareness, including an understanding of account budgets, resourcing and profitability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An established and growing network of business, policy and/or political contacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
